    "narrative": "The Austin Waves are primed for a high-ceiling performance today, headlined by **Gunnar Henderson** (81.88), whose matchup against Elder offers the most favorable combination of park factors and platoon advantage. He is closely followed by **Drake Baldwin** (71.83) and **Jacob Wilson** (71.63); both are locked into leadoff roles with substantial SP skill bonuses, providing excellent opportunities for run production. **Sam Antonacci** (67.67) also continues to be a high-upside play, leveraging a strong park and a leadoff spot to remain an essential component of our efficiency-focused build.\n\nOur optimization model leaned heavily into favorable matchups against pitchers with elevated xERAs, such as the trio of **Curtis Mead**, **Nasim Nunez**, and **Miguel Vargas**, who all draw matchups against Bratt or Brown and benefit from robust SP skill projections. The most difficult personnel decision involved **Brayan Rocchio**, who narrowly missed the cut at 51.97. While **Brayan Rocchio** possesses the requisite profile to provide value, he was squeezed out by the superior power-hitting metrics of **Dominic Smith** and the overall scoring efficiency of our starting infield. \n\nInvestors should monitor the volatility surrounding **Kyle Tucker** (51.42). Despite his pedigree, his score has been tempered by a tough encounter with McLean, whose elite arm forces a cautious outlook. We are also tracking **Liam Hicks** (56.65) carefully; while he remains a start, his low base projection suggests he is hovering near the lower threshold of our efficiency requirements. We are currently carrying **Luis Robert Jr.**, **Jordan Westburg**, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, **Josh Jung**, **Coby Mayo**, **Wade Meckler**, **Luis Lara**, and **Cole Carrigg** on the roster, though these assets remain on the periphery of today\u2019s specific daily efficiency targets.",
